{title: Way Maker}
{subtitle: Wegebner}
{song_number: 51}
{key: E}
{tempo: 68}
{language: en}

{comment: Verse 1}
[A]You are here, moving in our [E]midst; I worship You, [Bsus4]I worship You.
[C#m]You are here, working in this [E]place; I worship You, [Bsus4]I worship You.

{comment: Verse 2}
[A]You are here, touching ev'ry [E]heart; I worship You, [Bsus4]I worship You.
[C#m]You are here, healing ev'ry [E]heart; I worship You, [Bsus4]I worship You.

{comment: Verse 3}
[A]You are here, turning lives around; [E]I worship You, [Bsus4]I worship You.
[C#m]You are here, mending ev'ry [E]heart; I worship You, [Bsus4]I worship You.

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Way Maker, Miracle Worker,
[E]Promise Keeper, Light in the darkness.
[Bsus4]My God, that is who You are. [C#m]You are.
[A]That is who You are. [E]That is who You are.
[B]That is who You are. [C#m]That is who You are.
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Bridge 1}
[C#m]You wipe away all [E]tears. You mend the broken [A]heart.
[E]You're the answer to it all, [B]Jesus. [C#m]

{comment: Bridge 2}
[A]Even when I don't see it, You're working.
[E]Even when I don't feel it, You're working.
[Bsus4]You never stop, You never stop working.
[C#m]You never stop, You never stop working.
{comment: Order in score: verses and chorus; bridge 1; bridge 2 four times; D.S.S. al Fine.}
